# Cloudflare's header rules for the site's files (docs/decisions/2026-10-21-cloudflare-for-the-site.md).
# Vite names every file under /assets/ by its content's hash, so a file
# there never changes: a year, and the browser never asks again. The
# pictures below are asked again behind the drawing; everything else keeps
# Cloudflare's default (asked again each visit, a 304 when it's unchanged),
# as its name stays the same when it changes. Rules that match one path are
# merged, a header set twice joined with a comma: so no rule for /* sets
# Cache-Control, and no two that set it match one path
# (cloudflare/headers.test.js).
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The pictures the worlds draw with, whose names stay when they change (the
# universe map's planets and sky, the CC0 sets, the HDR skies, the fonts):
# stale at once, as the default has them, but a copy kept from the last week
# is drawn with straight away while the browser asks again behind it, so a
# returning visitor's world isn't waiting on hundreds of 304s before its
# first frame. A picture changed by a deploy is the old one for that one
# visit and the new one after. (The heavy files the bucket holds are a year
# already, their paths their hashes. Models are left out: the code that
# comes with a model reads its nodes' names, and a stale one could break
# that visit.) docs/decisions/2026-10-22-pictures-fresh-in-the-background.md
/textures/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/hdri/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/cc0/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, stale-while-revalidate=604800

# Any site may read the files, as GitHub Pages let it when it served the
# site (it sent this on every file): the Minecraft player, on an origin of
# its own, fetches the game's sealed file from /eagler/
# (public/eagler-player/index.html), and without it the game wouldn't open.
# A public site with no logins: nothing is given away. (A file there stays
# under Cloudflare's 25 MiB: 1.12.2.bin is 22.2.)
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
